The fix is complete. Here's a summary of what I did.

## The bug

When Babel transforms bundled code that carries an input source map (with a `names` array), and a plugin renames a variable to a conflict-avoiding name (e.g. inner `root` → `root2$$$`), the output source map was recording the *renamed* name (`root2$$$`) instead of tracing back to the original name (`root`) stored in the input map.

## Root cause

In `packages/babel-generator/src/source-map.ts`, the `mark()` method looked up the original position in the input map via `originalPositionFor`, but **it never used the `name` recorded there**. It only consulted the input map's name in the narrow `(`‑method‑head case (`identifierNamePos`). For a plain renamed identifier, it fell through and emitted whatever name the AST carried — the renamed one. The stale comment even said *"if we found a name, nothing else needs to be done"*, incorrectly assuming the AST name was already correct.

## The fix

Prefer the input map's name (`originalMapping.name`) when marking an identifier, guarded so it's only trusted when the mapping actually corresponds to that token:

```js
if (
  originalMapping.name &&
  (identifierNamePos ||
    (identifierName != null && originalMapping.column === column))
) {
  identifierName = originalMapping.name;
} else if (identifierNamePos) {
  // ...existing `(`-method-head fallback lookup
}
```

The `originalMapping.column === column` guard is the key subtlety: it only adopts the input map's name when the mapping lines up exactly with the marked position (the genuine chained-identifier case), avoiding pulling a name from an unrelated, coarser mapping onto a different token — which is what happens with things like arrow-function desugaring maps.

## Verification
- Reproduced the bug (renamed `root2$$$` mapping to `root2$$$` in output names), then confirmed the fix produces `names: ["marker","root","outer","test","inner"]` with each renamed identifier tracing back to `root`, plus `ignoreList: []`, `version`, `sources`, `sourcesContent` all preserved.
- Full `@babel/generator` suite: **1735 passed** (including the previously-at-risk `inputSourceMap without sourcesContent` arrow-function test, which the column guard protects).
- `@babel/core` source-map tests pass. The only failing suite (`esm-cjs-integration`) fails identically before my change — it's an environmental browserslist/caniuse-lite stderr warning, unrelated to source maps.

I did not touch anything under `tests/`, and only modified the source file `packages/babel-generator/src/source-map.ts`.

Sources: [Names missing from source map · babel#9173](https://github.com/babel/babel/issues/9173), [Source-map name mappings · babel#15647](https://github.com/babel/babel/issues/15647)
